ates to  have previously held an elected position  want to know your opinion Thanks yeah  it's not a good idea so number one I  think it would be politically impossible  quite frankly to pass a constitutional  amendment that would codify that to be  President you not only have to be of a  certain age and born in a certain way  and the few requirements that are there  but that you also need to have held some  kind of elected position and there's a  few problems with it number one it  you're simply not going to get agreement  on that but it is such an amorphous  designation what counts right you then  get into the position of having to say  well okay senator counts governor  accounts a congressman or congresswoman  counts but what about the mayor of a  town or city well okay it should count  if it's mayor of New York City but it  shouldn't if it's a really small city  what about being elected as a city  councilor somewhere it's it's not a good  idea and I think we would be much better  off building a society in which you  don't need such a restriction people  realized why it's a terrible idea to  elect someone like Donald Trump without  having him be disqualified  constitutionally because he hasn't held  elected office I think that's the wrong  way forward I don't think it's really in  line with the ideas of what the United  States of America is so I think we're  way better off using voter turnout and  critical thinking and understandings of  history and economics and science and  everything else to come to the  conclusion that you've got to have  something pretty wrong with you or be a  bad person or be extraordinarily  ignorant to vote for someone like Donald  Trump I wouldn't do it via a  constitutional amendment I think it's a  bad idea I don't think it would work  either we've got a great bonus show for  you today we'll talk about how much the  health care industry spends on marketing  money which could be saved if we had a  different type of health care system w